  "text_md": "# Table 30. Reserved Variable Names\n\nThe date the Print Database File Member job is requested.\n\n*DATE\n\nThe time the Print Database File Member job is requested.\n\n*TIME\n\nThe number of the page on which the record is printed.\n\n*PAGNBR\n\n*RCDNBR\n\nThe record number within the database file.\n\nThe name of the database file to be printed.\n\nDBFIL\n\nThe library name of the database file:\n\nDBLIB\n\nThe name of the member to be printed.\n\nDBMBR\n\nTo select reserved variable names, press the F4 on the Define Text Detail (or the Define Box Detail) display The following display appears: key\n\n![](<6b66abea2ba083424a4f099edb1b604e92d79a9a0c491b175da320b8ad7be457_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nSelect Field in Record Format Database file . . . . . . : MLTFMT Library . . . . . . . . : SENDAI Record Format . . . . . . : MLTFMT Type an option, press Enter. 1=Select Opt Field Length Type Text AREA 8 C Area products developed PRICE 3 P Price of the product PRODCT 12 C Product name SIZE 4 P Size Bottom F5=Refresh F11=Select reserved variable F12=Cancel\n\nThen press the FlI The following display appears: key\n\n![](<6b66abea2ba083424a4f099edb1b604e92d79a9a0c491b175da320b8ad7be457_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\n# Select Reserved Variable Name\n\nType option, press 1=Select\n\nEnter.\n\n1-Select\n\nOpt\n\nReserved variable name *DATE\n\nDescription Job date Job time Page number Record number Database file name Database library name Database member name\n\n- *DATE\n- *TIME\n- *PAGNBR\n- *RCDNBR\n- *DBFIL\n- *DBLIB\n- *DBMBR\n\n\nF5=Refresh F11=Select field F12=Cancel\n\n",
